Third-party components
----------------------

This repository contains no vendored third-party source code and no
installed dependencies. The optional rc-admin template
(`templates/tooling/rc-admin/`) declares the following npm dependencies.
The consumer installs them from the public npm registry under their own
licenses; they are not redistributed in this repository.

    express                 MIT
    firebase-admin          Apache-2.0
    dotenv                  BSD-2-Clause
    google-auth-library     Apache-2.0

`templates/tooling/rc-admin/package-lock.json` is a lockfile: it records
package names, versions, and integrity hashes only, not package source.

The `rc-admin` template connects to Firebase using the public OAuth client
that ships inside the `firebase-tools` npm package, which is why those
client identifiers appear in `credentials.js`. They are not secrets and
grant no access without your own Firebase project credentials.
